{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he encountered the place.</b> The plain sense of Scripture is that he encountered a certain settled place, and as you will find, Scripture concludes its statement at the end, as it is written: ״וְאוּלָם לוּז שֵׁם הָעִיר״ (Genesis 28:19) — see, it was a city, and he lodged there in that city." "And its saying <b>for the sun had set</b> is to say that were it not for this, he would have continued going to reach the destination of his desire, in fulfillment of his father's and mother's command. And our Rabbis of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 68:9) interpreted it as referring to the known place, Mount Moriah, as it is written (Genesis 22:4): ״וַיַּרְא אֶת הַמָּקוֹם״ etc., and this is the way of derash through the point of the letter heh. And their words of blessed memory are as written and as transmitted to us, and there is no contradiction to our interpretation, as Rashi explained that Mount Moriah was uprooted and came there, for this is that place — the holy place." "<b>And he lay down in that place.</b> Scripture informs this in order to say ״וַיַּחֲלוֹם״ etc., and it says <b>in that place</b>, because the lying down is not the thing that brings about the dream, but rather because of that place — for it was a holy place, as it says at the end." "<b>Further,</b> it alludes in its saying <b>and he lay down in the place</b> in accordance with what they of blessed memory said (Ḥullin 91b) that the earth folded under him. Therefore it says ״וַיִּשְׁכַּב בַּמָּקוֹם הַהוּא״ — meaning, in its entirety he lay in it, as it says (Genesis 28:13): ״אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה שׁוֹכֵב עָלֶיהָ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:15.488867299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}